# Vendor source checkouts (can be huge)
**/source/

# Metasploit dev environment
msf-modules/
msf-init.rc
msf-lab.sh
docker-compose.msf.yml
metasploit/

# Internal docs/reports (local only). Anchored to the repository root so the
# rule does not also swallow every vendored `docs/` directory inside a CVE
# package (e.g. boringssl's third_party/googletest/docs/).
/docs/
.claude/
BYPASS_FINDINGS_LOG.md
INDEX.md

# Local docker helper scripts
WORKING-DOCKER.md
check-all-docker.sh

# Docker/lab runtime artifacts
**/.env
# v4 pipeline packages deliberately ship a reviewed lab-only .env
!CVE-*/.env
**/.env.control
**/reg-page-id.txt
*.log
*.pid
**/data/
# Anchored to the repository root, like docs/ above: an unanchored **/logs/
# also matched vendored logs/ directories inside a CVE package (openlitespeed's
# dist/lsns/logs and test/serverroot/logs), which then could not be published.
/logs/
poc-run-logs/
poc-run-results.md
runtime-ports.env
runtime-ports.md
.docker-compose.verify.yml
.runtime-port-map.csv
pipeline-run-report.md
/templates/
RUN-DOCKER-SINGLE.md

# Internal tooling — not part of the CVE collection itself
/.skills/
